<section class="tight" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="card rv" id="why">
      <p class="eyebrow">Channel policy &middot; 2026</p>
      <h2 class="t-2" style="margin-top:14px;max-width:20ch">Why the prices differ between them.</h2>
      <p class="sm" style="margin-top:18px;max-width:72ch">A product on a chemist's shelf carries costs an online listing doesn't &mdash; distributor margin, retailer margin, stock credit, returns. When the same brand appears online cheaper, the retailer who stocked it loses, and eventually stops stocking it.</p>
      <p class="sm" style="margin-top:14px;max-width:72ch">So we separated them. <strong>Ascovita</strong> is made for the trade and priced to protect it. <strong>Ascofizz</strong> is made for online, with its own SKUs and pack sizes. Same facility, same formulations team, same release testing &mdash; two identities, so neither channel undercuts the other.</p>
